Z||000006||ounmongk||03-25-2000||05:36 PM||||hey guys,<BR>doughboy, yeah I saw those pics of your car before, I wanted to comment on a job well done, but my damn computer didn't seem to want to cooperate.(21st century and everything still doesn't work!)  anyways... how much leg room did you lose from that box? <BR>looks pretty minimal... what's your email so that I can get those specs?Thanks a bunch... overlord, keep us up to date on the job.. I wonder what 2 10" would be like... geez I can't wait to lose my hearing. (just turn it up louder!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks again guys||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||03-25-2000||06:50 PM||||overlord--The double firewall is the carpeted piece right behind the seats.  If it's not there, someone's removed it from your car (can't see why someone would do that, though).<P>A friend made an interesting suggestion the other day.  Why not put the sub behind the drivers seat??  Most want the feeling of the bass at least as much as the actual sound.  Makes sense to me.||||reg||1
Z||000008||phillip||03-25-2000||09:28 PM|||| two things. there is a company called illusion audio that makes a sub that is fairly shallow (neodymium magnet that sits in front of the cone).pretty costly though, but maybe you could make a tall thin box with them. also you could try some bass shakers. pretty much they are tranducers that vibrate with the music. you hook them up and cross them over like subs. about the size of a speaker magnet, maybe you could put one behind each seat. you still need a sub but maybe you could use a smaller one up front to go with them.the down side of that is you need either two amps,one for the shakers and one for the sub, or one 8ohm speaker run parallel with the shakers run in series ( to keep a 4ohm impedance with a bridged amp,unless you're using a high current amp) or two 4ohm and two shakers.that way tou could run a shaker and a sub on each channel or bridge the amp and run them all together series parallel. that got complicated but you can see there are other options. in the future i can tell you more about the shakers. i have a pair in another car but i'm still working on the system.||||reg||1
Z||000009||doughboySE||03-25-2000||10:42 PM||||hehehe stupid me<BR>doughboy@sprint.ca<BR>well i would imagine i lost 6 inches but im 6 foot and the only problem i have is getting in but i have that problem on the drivers side as well <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)))))) once your in you have plenty of leg room and i love the idea that i f i want to take it out then its out just 2 wires to unplug<BR>anyway mail me i have the specs right here i measured today and thanx for the compliment||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||03-26-2000||11:27 AM||||Phillip, I can vouch for the bass shakers in fieros. I have a set in mine. I would not recommend mounting behind the seat, as you must remove carpeting to mount them.  I removed a 12" square of carpeting under the seats and have very good shakin.  I am looking at Bazooka 6.5" tube to see if it will in stock subwoofer location. I'll keep y'all posted.||||reg||1
